        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Longshan culture</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The middle and lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> valley of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> (Chengziya, near the town of Longshan in Zhangqiu; Liangchengzhen and Yaowangcheng on the Rizhao coast), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> (Taosi in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fen-river">Fen River</a> valley) and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 3000–1900 BCE: an early Miaodigou II phase (3000–2600 BCE) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, then a late period (2600–2000 BCE) of regional variants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> or “classic” Longshan, Wangwan III, Hougang II, Taosi, Sanliqiao II and Kexingzhuang II (the Shaanxi Longshan); decline towards the end of the 3rd millennium BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">thin-walled, highly polished black “egg-shell” pottery made on the wheel; rammed-earth town walls; centres of over 200 hectares such as Taosi; divination with heated shoulder blades; the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> area; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> tools, rings and bells; jade prestige goods; small-scale <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> production</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Chengziya site, found in 1928 and excavated in 1930 and 1931; excavations at Shanxian in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> in the 1950s; regional surveys of settlement hierarchies; plant and animal remains and skeletons; syntheses by Kwang-chih Chang (1963, 1986), Yan Wenming and others.</span></div>
        </div>
